{
  "message": "The strongest current sign-up offer I found is the EcoCard: spend at least $5,000 in eligible purchases during your first month and earn 2,000 sustainability points. The offer runs through December 15, 2025, and the account must be new, open, and in good standing when the bonus is awarded. The points redeem at $0.01 each, so the bonus is worth $20 as a statement or checking-account credit. Exclusions include balance transfers, cash equivalents, fees, returns, chargebacks, and disputed transactions.",
  "comparison": [
    {
      "card": "EcoCard",
      "sign_up_offer": "2,000 sustainability points after $5,000 in eligible first-month spending",
      "approximate_value": "$20",
      "annual_fee": "$50",
      "apr": "19.99%"
    },
    {
      "card": "Business Silver Rewards Card",
      "sign_up_offer": "2x cash back for the first 6 months",
      "eligibility": "Business applicants",
      "offer_status": "The listed offer ends November 14, 2025; confirm availability before applying"
    },
    {
      "card": "Gold Rewards Card",
      "sign_up_offer": "No sign-up bonus was listed in the available information",
      "ongoing_rewards": "2.5% cash back on all purchases",
      "requirements": "Minimum credit score of 720 and an active Rho-Bank+ subscription"
    }
  ],
  "recommendation": "If your priority is specifically a sign-up bonus and you can comfortably meet the spending requirement, the EcoCard is the best documented current option. If you prefer ongoing cash back rather than a sign-up bonus, the Gold Rewards Card offers 2.5% cash back on all purchases, subject to its requirements.",
  "follow_up": "Are you looking for a personal or business card, and approximately how much could you spend during the first month?"
}

{
  "message": "Since you are unsure you can spend $5,000 in the first month, I would not recommend applying for the EcoCard solely for its sign-up offer. You should count only planned, eligible purchases you can comfortably pay for; do not spend extra to reach the threshold. The offer requires $5,000 within one month, and the 2,000-point bonus is worth about $20, while the card has a $50 annual fee.",
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "card": "Silver Rewards Card",
      "why_it_may_fit": "No annual fee, 0% introductory APR for the first year, and 1% cash back on purchases outside its top categories",
      "requirements": "Minimum credit score of 680",
      "sign_up_bonus": "No sign-up bonus was listed in the available information"
    },
    {
      "card": "Bronze Rewards Card",
      "why_it_may_fit": "No annual fee and 0% introductory APR for the first year, with a lower stated credit-score requirement",
      "requirements": "Minimum credit score of 640",
      "sign_up_bonus": "No sign-up bonus was listed in the available information"
    },
    {
      "card": "Gold Rewards Card",
      "why_it_may_fit": "2.5% cash back on all purchases",
      "requirements": "Minimum credit score of 720 and an active Rho-Bank+ subscription",
      "sign_up_bonus": "No sign-up bonus was listed in the available information"
    }
  ],
  "recommendation": "If avoiding an uncertain spending target is most important, the Silver Rewards Card is the most balanced personal option among the documented cards: no annual fee, a first-year 0% introductory APR, and ongoing cash back. Choose the Bronze Rewards Card if your likely credit score is closer to 640–679. Consider the EcoCard only if you already expect at least $5,000 of eligible first-month purchases and accept its $50 annual fee.",
  "next_step": "Before applying, estimate your unavoidable first-month purchases—such as bills, groceries, or planned expenses—and compare that amount with the EcoCard's $5,000 requirement."
}
